# Data

**Color:** `#6C5CE7` | **Nodes:** 9

The Data category provides nodes for parsing, serializing, and reading/writing structured data.

## JSON

**Color:** `#6C5CE7`

| Type | Node Name | Inputs | Outputs | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `data/json/parse` | Parse JSON | json(String) | object(JSON), error(String) | Parse a JSON string into an object |
| `data/json/get` | JSON Get | object(JSON), key(String) | value(Generic) | Extract a value from a JSON object by key |
| `data/json/set` | JSON Set | object(JSON), key(String), value(Generic) | result(JSON) | Set a value in a JSON object by key |
| `data/json/array` | JSON Array | items(Array) | json(JSON) | Convert an array to a JSON array |

### Example Uses

```
API Response → [Parse JSON] → [JSON Get] → [Display]   // Extract field from JSON
[Object] [Key] [Value] → [JSON Set] → [File Writer]     // Modify and save JSON
```

## Serialization

**Color:** `#A29BFE`

| Type | Node Name | Inputs | Outputs | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `data/serialization/serialize` | Serialize Object | object(Generic) | json(String) | Convert any object to its JSON string representation |
| `data/serialization/deserialize` | Deserialize Object | json(String) | object(Map) | Parse JSON string back into a map object |

### Example Uses

```
[Node data] → [Serialize Object] → [File Writer]     // Export graph data as JSON
[File Reader] → [Deserialize Object] → [JSON Get]     // Load and query data
```

## File I/O

**Color:** `#00CEC9`

| Type | Node Name | Inputs | Outputs | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `data/file/read` | Read File | path(String) | content(String), success(Bool) | Read file contents from disk |
| `data/file/write` | Write File | path(String), content(String) | success(Bool) | Write content to a file on disk |
| `data/file/csvParse` | CSV Parse | csv(String), separator(String) | rows(Array) | Parse CSV text into an array of rows |

### Example Uses

```
"data.csv" → [Read File] → [CSV Parse] → [Bar Chart]   // Load CSV and chart it
[Content] [Path] → [Write File] → [Boolean Indicator]    // Save file / check success
```
